From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:19:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Smarter visuals: vision-ranked stock + fully-generated AI
 b-roll
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vision-ranked stock (the 'AI finds the RIGHT footage' fix):
- Stock candidates now carry thumbnail frames (Pexels/Pixabay)
- One vision call shows the tenant's text model every candidate thumbnail
  plus the narrated scenes and asks it to assign the best-matching clip to
  each scene (meaning over keywords, variety preferred, watermarks avoided)
- Successful rankings pin each sentence to its clip via the sceneMap;
  failed downloads fall back per scene; ranking is STRICTLY fail-soft —
  any error/timeout/non-vision model reverts to the old search order
- Fixes irrelevant footage, especially for non-English topics whose
  translated search terms match poorly

AI b-roll (visualsSource 'ai') — owned imagery, zero licensing questions:
- One LLM art-direction call writes a photorealistic prompt per scene
  (consistent mood, no text/watermarks), images generated through the
  existing switchable imageGen registry (concurrency 3)
- Each still becomes a Ken Burns clip sized to its scene, composed with
  the normal narration/subtitles/ducked-music pipeline
- Priced at 2 video units per paragraph (half the character rate: images
  only, no image-to-video calls); 15-minute deadline tier
- Contract enum + UI toggle ('AI imagery') with cost note

Deliberately NOT web scraping: scraped media in customers' published
marketing posts is a copyright/DMCA liability. Ranked licensed pools +
generated imagery deliver the relevance without the risk.

Tests: Ken Burns stillToClip (real ffmpeg), ai/character/stock unit
pricing, ranking fail-soft guarantees; 63 API + 9 page tests green;
typecheck + spec lint + codegen drift clean.

